<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Control Instruments pulls out of buy.</title>
<headline>Control Instruments pulls out of buy.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's Control Instruments Group Ltd said on Friday that it had decided not to go ahead with a planned buy of an unnamed firm.</p>
<p>The group said the decision was taken following a due diligence investigation.</p>
<p>Control Instruments first announced it was in talks on a buy in December and its shares had been trading under a cautionary notice since that date.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
